    skos:broader attack-detection:DET0241 ;
    skos:definition "Detects forged Kerberos Silver Tickets by identifying anomalous Kerberos service ticket activity such as malformed fields in logon events, TGS requests without interaction with the KDC, and access attempts using service accounts outside expected hosts/resources. Also monitors suspicious processes accessing LSASS memory for credential dumping."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/crgo/vocab/attack-detection> ;
    skos:notation "AN0675" ;
    skos:note "Log sources: WinEventLog:Security [EventCode=4672, 4634]; WinEventLog:Kerberos [Kerberos TGS-REQ anomalies without KDC validation (Silver Ticket behavior)]; WinEventLog:Sysmon [EventCode=10]"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analytic 0675 (Windows)"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000283 crgo:CRGO_0000069 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000284 crgo:CRGO_0000063 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000286 "MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise 19.2 STIX bundle"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000288 crgo:CRGO_0000181 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000289 crgo:CRGO_0000182 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000290 "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000291 "0.10.0" ;
    crgo:CRGO_0001243 attack-detection:DC0035,
        attack-detection:DC0084,
        attack-detection:DC0088 .

attack-detection:AN0676 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0242#AN0676> ;
    skos:broader attack-detection:DET0242 ;
    skos:definition "Unusual database command-line access (e.g., `psql`, `mysql`, `mongo`) from non-admin users, occurring outside typical automation windows or without known service context. Often followed by data dumps to .sql/.csv files or outbound data transfers. Defender sees CLI tools launched interactively or by unusual parent processes, file writes to dump-like filenames, and external connections shortly after."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/crgo/vocab/attack-detection> ;
    skos:notation "AN0676" ;
    skos:note "Log sources: auditd:SYSCALL [execve: Execution of CLI tools like psql, mysql, mongo, sqlite3]; auditd:PATH [Creation of files with extensions .sql, .csv, .sqlite, especially in user directories]; NSM:Flow [http::post: Outbound HTTP POST from host shortly after DB export activity]"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analytic 0676 (Linux)"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000283 crgo:CRGO_0000069 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000284 crgo:CRGO_0000063 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000286 "MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise 19.2 STIX bundle"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000288 crgo:CRGO_0000181 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000289 crgo:CRGO_0000182 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000290 "2026-10-13"^^xsd:date ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000291 "0.10.0" ;
    crgo:CRGO_0001243 attack-detection:DC0032,
        attack-detection:DC0039,
        attack-detection:DC0085 .

attack-detection:AN0677 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0242#AN0677> ;
    skos:broader attack-detection:DET0242 ;
    skos:definition "Database client execution (e.g., sqlcmd.exe, isql.exe) by users or from locations not tied to enterprise automation or backups. Often followed by creation of .sql/.bak/.csv files, registry artifacts for ODBC/JDBC drivers, or encrypted ZIPs. Defender sees SQL tools launched by explorer.exe, Powershell, or odd parent processes, plus file writes in user temp locations."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/crgo/vocab/attack-detection> ;
    skos:notation "AN0677" ;
    skos:note "Log sources: WinEventLog:Security [EventCode=4688]; WinEventLog:Sysmon [EventCode=11]; WinEventLog:Sysmon [EventCode=3, 22]"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Analytic 0677 (Windows)"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000283 crgo:CRGO_0000069 ;
