    rdfs:seeAlso <https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0080> ;
    skos:definition """The initiation or activation of a virtual machine instance within a cloud infrastructure. This action typically involves starting an existing instance that had been stopped or paused, allowing it to resume operation. Examples: 

- Google Cloud Platform (GCP): Starting an instance through `instance.start` API activity.
- AWS: Logging of `StartInstances` in AWS CloudTrail for EC2 instances.
- Azure: `Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/start` entries indicate a VM instance being started."""@en ;
